# Client structure

Read `docs/PAGE_VIEWS.md`, `docs/CARD_VIEWS.md`, and `docs/DIALOG_STRUCTURE.md` before adding a resource screen.

## Page and list

- `src/app/(app)/{resource}/page.tsx` imports `src/components/{resource}/list.tsx` and returns it. Do not fetch data or render tables in the page.
- The list is the client default export. It owns Redux loading, search, filters, sorting, pagination, and dialogs.
- Table columns live in `table-view/{resource}-table-columns.tsx`. The table view renders shared `TableView` with the rows and callbacks the list passes in. It does not load the list. Pagination stays on the list.
- A card view in `card-views/{resource}-cards.tsx` receives the same rows and callbacks. Add one only when the list toggles between `"table"` and `"cards"`.
- Keep `SearchFilterBar`, `Pagination`, `TableView`, and `CardActionsMenu` in `src/components/common`.

## Dialogs

- One file per screen: `create-{resource}-dialog.tsx` and `edit-{resource}-dialog.tsx`.
- Put the fields function in that same file. Do not add a `*-form.tsx`, and do not switch create and edit inside one dialog with a nullable id.
- The list uses `creating` and `editingId`. Edit dialogs take a required id.
- A different screen (receive, timeline, assign, delete, view) gets its own dialog file. Delete confirmation is `delete-{resource}-dialog.tsx`.
- Purchase-order create, edit, receive, and timeline stay separate. Use the four dialog files the purchase-order list imports.
